{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1182448-advice-on-a-indiana-jones-like-npc","id":1182448,"title":"Advice on a Indiana Jones- like NPC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-04T17:45:30-08:00","id":1182448,"title":"Advice on a Indiana Jones- like NPC","content":"I have a concept for a NPC for when I pick up Scion Origins. His name is Colonel John Heyward, a former British Army man and a well-known archeologist . My idea for this NPC is to make him famous for uncovering many artifacts around the world, many of them thought to be myths. The unusual part of this is the fact that he was over 50 years old when he made most of these discoveries. Heyward, as of this time, is in his early eighties and is yearning to go on another adventure, especially after being diagnosed with a brain tumor that will kill him in 3 years.<br /> <br /> \u200bThroughout the time the PCs get to know the Colonel, they will discover that his adventures are more action packed then they think, especially when one of Heyward's old enemies, Jerome Bluster, comes out of the woodwork and tries to have the Colonel killed while at a visit in Japan. They also discover that Heyward, despite being a elderly gentleman at this time, is still quite a capable fighter and is surprisingly agile too. My idea for a explanation is that he is surprisingly favored by a member of one of the Pantheons, who gave the old Army man his or her blessings, but is letting the tumor kill him so they can be entertained by the &quot;Colonel's Last Adventure.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bI want advice on determining how this character could work mechanically and how to justify his Divine Patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}